# Node
frontend/node_modules/
node_modules/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.env
venv/
.venv/
# .venv313/ and friends are ignored today only by a .gitignore pip writes
# inside the virtualenv. That is not a rule this repository controls.
.venv*/
*.egg-info/

# Build outputs
frontend/build/
dist/

# ML models — the working directory stays ignored...
backend/saved_models/*.pkl
backend/saved_models/*.joblib
# Written by every training run; the committed copies live in backend/seed/models/.
backend/saved_models/*.json

# ...but backend/seed/ is a deliberate, committed snapshot: the database and
# trained models baked into the deployed image so a host with no persistent disk
# comes up working instead of untrained. ~6.5MB, small enough for plain git.
!backend/seed/
!backend/seed/**

# Data
data/*.csv
data/*.json

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docker
*.log

# Secrets and local host links. `.env` alone missed every variant, and .vercel was
# only ignored under frontend/, so a `vercel link` at the repo root would have
# committed the org and project ids. This repo is public: the rule is that
# anything describing *this* deployment stays out of it.
.env.*
!.env.example
.vercel/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.ppk
# Registry and host credentials, which land in the working tree by accident
# more often than any of the above.
.npmrc
.netrc
_netrc
credentials.json
# `!frontend/**/*.key` used to sit here, un-ignoring private keys under
# frontend/. It protected nothing - no such file has ever been tracked - and
# on a public repository an exception that re-admits a key is worth deleting
# even when it is currently harmless.

# Runtime state. backend/dbdata/ is the container's live database and is created
# by any local run or a bare `docker run` with a bind mount; it is not the
# committed snapshot in backend/seed/.
backend/dbdata/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
# `*.db` was missing, and a developer's local database is the one file in
# this project that holds real subscriber addresses. The negation that
# follows keeps the committed seed snapshot, and has to come after the rule
# it undoes: in .gitignore the last matching line wins.
*.db
!backend/seed/*.db

# Saved third-party pages. pl_page.html was a scraping reference that sat in the
# repo unreferenced for months and carried three of the Premier League's own
# frontend API keys, including a Google one. Republishing someone else's keys is
# not ours to do, so saved pages stay local.
pl_page.html
*_page.html
scratch/

# QA screenshots. Regenerated by `npm run qa:responsive`; they are evidence of a
# run, not source, and a binary per page per viewport per run is not history
# anyone wants in a diff.
frontend/screenshots/
